Falsifies `system_tests::user::survey_tests::a_corpse_still_leaving_its_core_is_reaped_once_it_has_left`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is `reap_supervised` refusing a corpse its core has not yet switched away from, rather
than waiting for it. `reclaim_region`'s refuse phase declines to free a stack a core stands on, and
without the wait that refusal reaches the supervisor as `NotPermitted`.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(..REAP.., Ok(0), "a corpse still leaving its core was refused rather
than waited for; ...")`, with `left: Err(NotPermitted)` and the refusal printed as
`Resident { state: Dead, on_cpu: true, being_reaped: false }`. Confirmed red on 2026-10-22 (UTC)
on all three architectures at four cores with `NIFE_SMP=4 script/test --arch <arch> --test
a_corpse_still_leaving_its_core_is_reaped_once_it_has_left` (1 of 1 each).

